{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 9, :comments ["<b>And He said to him, 'Where are you?'</b> Meaning: why are you hiding and not showing yourself before Me? And he answered that he was afraid to stand before Him on account of seeing himself naked, and it is forbidden to stand before a Torah scroll naked — all the more so before the Master, blessed be He. And according to our interpretation in the verse ״וַתִּפָּקַחְנָה״ etc. — that they sensed their descent and their transgression — he answered that he was ashamed upon seeing himself naked, from the zohar of kedushah. Also according to the statement of our Sages, their memory for blessing (Bereshit Rabbah), that his royal garment had been stripped from him, he is speaking of his being literally naked — for did He not sew for him a fig leaf?"], :book :genesis, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 3, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:38:40.707938738Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}